{"full":"hf:chinmaypala/claude_hackathon","spaceId":"chinmaypala/claude_hackathon","name":"Variant-Screening Workbench","source":"huggingface","description":"An interactive AI application on Hugging Face Spaces.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":null,"topics":["docker","region:us"],"technologies":[],"likes":3,"created":"2026-07-08T00:06:16.000Z","updated":"2026-07-10T00:26:19.000Z","license":null,"runtime":"SLEEPING","appUrl":"https://chinmaypala-claude-hackathon.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/chinmaypala/claude_hackathon","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T18:59:37.008Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T18:59:37.008Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T18:59:37.008Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🧬","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A terminal-native workbench that takes a protein and a plain-language goal, triages what kind of campaign it can run, drives an iterative loop that proposes and ranks variants, and ends at a finished design you take to a cloud lab.","When a registered combinatorial DMS landscape exists for the protein (GB1), the loop returns real assayed fitness. When no measured landscape exists, it runs a predict-only loop that ranks variants by computable in silico proxies, clearly labeled predicted rather than measured.","Framing rule: proposal and modeling run in silico. Measured values are real prior measurements from a published deep mutational scan, standing in for a live bench round; predicted values are in silico estimates and are labeled as such. Nothing here implies benchtop validation that did not happen, and the pipeline never places a lab order on its own."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/chinmaypala/claude_hackathon/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"94eb458ca16ce6cff79592faaee900676de651e129f2ca76f87e9f2ffd9a262f","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T18:59:37.046Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T18:59:37.046Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"wh